Author: moritztng <moritztng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Aug 10 13:21:41 2026 +0000

    fix(protenix): fall back to ttnn's own matmul planner when the tuned config clashes
    
    `_batched_matmul_search` budgets its circular buffers against `get_max_worker_l1_unreserved_size()`
    on an idle device, so it cannot see what the live block is already holding. When the sum overflows
    the 1 461 760 B bank the clash is raised at program compile inside tt-metal, not by the allocator,
    and the fold dies. FIX-D removes the co-residency that made the whole [385, 506] token band throw;
    this closes the gate that admitted the config in the first place.
    
    Same contract as `_L1_OUT_REFUSED`, which has solved exactly this for the pair-track output
    projections since dafd49c1: attempt the tuned config once per shape class, catch the throw, memoise
    the refusal, and use `program_config=None` for the rest of the process. One caught exception per
    class rather than one per call, so a fold that refuses pays microseconds and not the 12 576 x 357 us
    it would cost unmemoised.
    
    The fallback is arithmetically safe: `program_config=None` hands the same operands to ttnn's own
    planner. `per_core_M` and `block_w` trade occupancy and in1 re-reads; `in0_block_w` is the only
    field that regroups the accumulation, and a config that never ran cannot have set it.
    
    Also records `_L1_OUT_REFUSED`, `_BMM_CFG_REFUSED` and the live per-bank L1 view per fold in
    perf/zsize/sweep_qb1.py, and commits the FIX-D hunk as a patch so a run can toggle it.

